Pin the socket contract and corpus; correct platform and parity claims

spec/ now also carries the retiring socket contract (sophia-shell-v1.kdl)
and Sophia's shell golden corpora, all in SHA256SUMS, and
sophia-shell-ipc's corpus test decodes and re-encodes them standalone.
The crate's doc now names the real parity test in Sophia instead of
claiming one. PLATFORMS.md claims Linux x86_64 only; aarch64 is expected
to work but untested.
